  "question": {
    "text": "Let for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo><mo>,</mo><mn>50</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mi>n</mi></msub></math>&nbsp;be the sum of the infinite geometric progression whose first term is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>&nbsp;and whose common ratio is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></math>. Then the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>26</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><munderover><mo>&#8721;</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>50</mn></munderover><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;is equal to"
  },
